    rdfs:label "Evidence for Honey used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 24"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "It grows like oats, but in quality resembles rice. ÆGYPTIACUM, a name formerly given to several medicinal preparations, the only one of which now in use is that called mel ægyptiacum, which is composed of honey and verdigris."@en ;
